WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.534
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.437
you know from "The Daily Show"
and "The Opposition."

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.373
He co-hosts the podcast
"Kasich &amp; Klepper,"

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.542
and his new special,
"The Daily Show with Trevor Noah

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.212
Presents Jordan Klepper
Fingers The Globe:

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.982
Hungry for Democracy," premieres
April 21st on Comedy Central.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.250
Let's take a look.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.685
-Were Hungarian rallies
anything like MAGA ones?

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.721
Do you have any Orban pictures,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.691
specifically with him shirtless,
riding a velociraptor?

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.092
-Just the flags.
That's basically

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:28.561
a Hungarian reference.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.797
-Does that have any profanity
on it whatsoever?

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.065
-No, it's just a --
-Just a straight flag.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.934
-Just a straightforward flag.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.136
[ Crowd chanting
in native language ]

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.671
-Lock her up!

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.840
[ Silence ]

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.375
I thought I heard,
"Lock her up."

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.843
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.645
our friend Jordan Klepper,
everybody.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.147
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:56.822 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.024
-How are you?

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.392
-Good, Seth!
How are you, sir?

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.760
-Good. I want to ask about
the podcast and the special,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.097
but I also want to ask,
you had a baby.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.431
Congratulations.
-Yes! Thank you very much.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.166
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:11.137
-And maybe the most stressful
time to have one,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.538
right at the beginning
of the pandemic.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.340
-Yes, exactly.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.309
And for the man especially,
it was really difficult for me.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.677
-Yeah, really.
And tonight, you know,

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.680
if we could take anything
away from today,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.315
it's men's rights and --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:25.819
-Exactly. Let's talk about
the male experience,

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.586
having a child during COVID.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.088
I'm so glad
I get an opportunity.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:32.358
No, it was incredibly stressful.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.993
And we were
right in the heart of it,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.430
so we didn't know if I'd get to
be in the delivery room or not.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.733
And we headed to the hospital,
and we arrive upon,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.636
right next to Central Park,
on the Upper East Side.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.005
And when you go in there,
usually the dad

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.142
can hang out in the lobby.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.443
-As they run the tests
or what have you,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.046
go into triage,
which is a very scary word.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.514
When they said,
"She's going into triage,"

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.215
I'm like, "Oh, my God!
Get the defibrillators!"

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.884
Like, "No, it's just a process."
Like, "Okay, I get that."

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:01.186
-You're like, "They have been
misusing it on TV."

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:03.189
-Yeah, "I have not been
paying attention to 'E.R.,'

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.691
clearly."
But they said,

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:07.226
"Well, we don't have
the space anymore,

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:09.428
so she's gonna go through there.
You have to wait outside.

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:11.264
There's no more common area."

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:14.166
So they sent me across the
street at midnight in New York.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:18.037
It was raining,
and I sat along Central Park.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.473
And if I looked down there,
about every 30 feet,

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:25.277
there was a man with a suitcase,
just waiting for their partner

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:27.146
inside to go through
all the hullabaloo.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.747
So it was a very --
-Aww.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:30.349
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.084
Again,
what the men have been through.

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:34.254
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.789
-Thank you, sir.
-We actually called your wife.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.257
We wanted her to be on the show
to tell her story,

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.358
and you answered and said,

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:40.692
"Mine's the story
you want to hear."

00:02:40.692 --> 00:02:42.928
-Yeah, yeah.
She's really busy.

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:46.498
I think enough people listened
to her side of things.

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:48.234
-Well, congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.738
-I'm glad it all worked out.
So, you have been, uh --

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.005
You do many things,
but you've been going

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.908
to a lot of Trump events.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:59.279
-And one of the things you do
that I think has made these

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:02.481
so enjoyable to watch is,
you very politely engage

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.951
with Trump supporters
and try to get to the bottom

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:08.655
of how they came to whatever
position it is they hold.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.922
-Yes.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.524
-When you go into it,
what do you set out to do?

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:14.060
I mean, do you have
a game plan in your head

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.928
of how you want to approach it?
-For sure.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.997
I mean, based on sort of
what is happening and what is

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.400
the news at the time,
we sort of break down,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.269
"Here are the narratives about
stories that are going on."

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.637
They're talking about CRT.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.505
We're reading people
talking about CRT.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.106
They're talking about
school-board meetings,

00:03:28.106 --> 00:03:29.775
they're stopping that.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.777
We'll go out with the narratives
we hear at home.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:35.247
We'll prep for perhaps responses
for those narratives.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:38.584
But when you arrive, you get
surprised just like that.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:41.120
You know, like, you can only
hear so many conspiracy theories

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.490
on television and then show up
and hear somebody say, you know,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.492
"The reason I keep 6 feet apart
from someone

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.193
is because
6 feet is the devil.

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:51.730
So therefore I won't be
listening to this devil sort of

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.199
spatial issues
that the government

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.633
wants to impose on me."
And you're like,

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.835
"That wasn't in my
'New York Times' this morning."

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.705
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.173
-So you kind of have to
drop everything.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:03.443
It's the improv rule of, like,
prep and then let it all go

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.645
and see what happens.
And more often than not,

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.348
it's just us pushing people
to get to the point

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.882
where they have to justify
the issues

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.417
they maybe
haven't thought through.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.786
-Right.
There is a core --

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.422
I know you to be a very nice,
very polite person in real life.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.124
You do bring that with you
to these rallies.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.959
Now, obviously,
you disagree with the people

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.462
you're engaging with,
but do you find it easy

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:27.100
to maintain what strikes me as,
like, a very affable persona

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.400
when you're talking to them?

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.537
-As a nice guy, is it easy to be
nice to these [bleep]?

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.838
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:35.108
These [bleep], man, these
[bleep], I gotta tell ya...

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.110
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.279
Well, it's infuriating,
I will say.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:44.083
Sometimes you want to
shake folks.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.784
I try not to.
Or babies.

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:47.220
Folks or babies.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.756
Again, good dad.
I've got dad brain.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:52.891
I will say,
what I empathize with

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:54.927
when I go to any of these
rallies is,

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.463
it's people want community.
And I get that.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.398
People want community,
and they need meaning.

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:01.334
And when you go to a rally,
what you find is

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.469
like-minded people
who have a purpose.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:06.705
And you walk into an arena
and you have the former leader

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:10.176
of the free world say, "You're
a hero, you're a patriot.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.978
Just do what I do."
And so I get that.

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.447
I joined an improv group.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.983
That gave me purpose
and a community.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.851
-Right.
-We all have our own cults.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.152
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:23.555
-So I can empathize with
why people are there, I think,

00:05:23.555 --> 00:05:26.292
but I get frustrated
with the logic

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.793
that's behind
some of these ideas.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.829
And the manipulation
of the people who impose

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.131
that logic onto these folks.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.934
-And you've obviously done
quite a few of these now.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.902
They're incredibly popular.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.906
You know, millions of people
have watched them.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:43.276
Are you recognizable now to some
people within that community?

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.978
-I am, yes.
I actually --

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.379
What's odd,
sometimes you get recognized,

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.315
and people want to engage.
Sometimes you get recognized,

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:52.218
and people want to yell at you
and chase you down.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:55.921
I went to CPAC recently,
and I was shocked because

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:58.557
I was prepared for people
to recognize me

00:05:58.557 --> 00:06:02.428
and not want to engage
and perhaps get fairly angry

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.430
that I was crashing their party.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.501
But I was shocked at how many
selfies I took at CPAC,

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:12.405
which is where conservatives go
to get their marching orders

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.873
for the next year.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:18.978
And what I quickly realized is,
I'm part of the narrative there.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:21.347
A little kid came up to me
who said he was -- a little kid?

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:22.481
He was, I think, 17.

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:23.950
He said he was
Trump's biggest fan.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.885
He showed me pictures
of mannequins he had

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.554
at home of Trump.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.990
He loved Trump.
He watched all my videos.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.525
And I asked him like, "Do you
see what I do in these videos?

00:06:33.525 --> 00:06:34.994
Why are you a fan?"

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:38.797
He's like, "I watch
all Trump stuff -- good, bad.

00:06:38.797 --> 00:06:40.199
It's all part of this world."

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:43.502
And even though I might be
espousing some points of view

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:47.439
that he doesn't agree with,
I'm the heel in this WWE world,

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:49.508
and, like, he needs me.
-Yeah.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:52.211
-And so he might be mildly
aggressive towards me,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.279
but beyond that,
he's more excited to actually

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:56.115
get this close to the world.
-Wow.

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:58.550
Do you think maybe a Jordan
mannequin's in his future?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.919
-God, I hope so.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:02.855
-Yeah. Do whatever you want
with it, kids.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.190
If you got a mannequin of me
at home, I'm not gonna judge.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.259
[ Laughter ]
Have fun.

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:08.560
-I want to talk about your trip
to Hungary.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.530
We'll be right back with more
from Jordan Klepper.

